=== LITEM Shadow
The black claw of the shadow
They say that from a slain shadow their restless soul enters them. Mages will gladly purchase them.

=== LITEM Shadow00
Black Witch claw
The only physical part of shadow. Used in magical rituals.

=== LITEM Shadow00_2
Black sorcerer claw
They say when restless souls leave killed shadows, they settle in these claws. Magicians will always buy them.

=== LITEM Shadow00_3
Black seer claw
A necessary element of magical rituals for casting certain spells.

=== LITEM Shadow00_4
Black magician claw
They say it is used for casting the most powerful spells...

=== LITEM SpiderSting
Sting of young spider
In crushed form they are used to make drugs and paints.

=== LITEM SpiderSting_2
Sting of spider
They are cheap but are widely used, so they are always in demand.

=== LITEM SpiderSting_3
Sting of large spider
Crushed spider stings are popular among ageing noblemen - apparently they bring back youth.

=== LITEM Spider_1
Stingers of a young spider
Crushed are suitable for medicines and antidotes.

=== LITEM Spider_2
Spider stingers
They're worth very little but have a wide range of uses, so the demand for them is relentless.

=== LITEM Spider_3
The stingers of a large spider
Rubbed spider stings are popular with aging women. They are believed to restore youth.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen
The head of an adult harpy
It can be purchased for a friendly joke. Although the joke will not be cheap.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00
Head of young harpy
A scarecrow like that set in front of the gates would keep more than just thieves away.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00_2
Head of harpy
This head on a spike in front of the gates would serve as a fair warning to criminals.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00_3
Head of adult harpy
It can be bought for a practical joke. It would be an expensive one, though.

=== LITEM SuccubusGreen00_4
Head of old harpy
Many a collector is combing the markets for a trophy like that.

=== LITEM SuccubusJ
The head of an adult harpy
It can be purchased for a friendly joke. Although the joke will not be cheap.


=== LITEM SuccubusRed
The head of an adult red harpy
Such a head on a pole in front of the village gate will scare away other harpies.

=== LITEM SuccubusRed00
Head of young red harpy
A head like that on a spike in front of the village gates would keep other Harpies away.

=== LITEM SuccubusRed00_2
Head of red harpy
Brigands would never venture into a village if they saw a head like this on a spike, right in front of the gates...

=== LITEM SuccubusRed00_3
Head of adult red harpy
If you see this on a spike in front of the gates, you know not to quarrel with the locals.

=== LITEM TigerS
Tiger skin
The entire skin of a giant tiger is a very valuable commodity.

=== LITEM Toad2_J
Legs of a large gray frog
Meat from the feet of a large gray toad counts as a delicacy.

=== LITEM ToadLegs00
Small Toad legs
Toads may spit poison but their meat is quite edible, so there is always a demand for it.

=== LITEM ToadLegs00_2
Toad legs
They pay good money for these: a nice addition to the family table.

=== LITEM ToadLegs00_3
Fat Toad legs
Legs of grown Toads are tender, considered a delicacy and cost good money.

=== LITEM Toad_1
The legs of a small toad
Although the toad spits venom, its meat is edible, and people will happily buy it.

=== LITEM Toad_2
Toad's legs
You'll get paid good money for it. It's a tasty addition to the family table.

=== LITEM Toad_3
The legs of a fat toad
There is more meat in the legs of an adult toad and they are non-venomous, so they are worth decent money.
=== LITEM Toad_4
Legs of the fat toad
The legs of an adult toad are delicate, so they count as a rarity and are worth a great deal.

=== LITEM Toad_J
Legs of the gray frog
The meat from the feet of the little gray toad is edible, but unpalatable.

